  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 6003.04 Fire Investigators and Fire Inspectors",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 6003.04 Fire Investigators and Fire Inspectors.\n\n(a) Fire investigators and fire inspectors, under the direction of the state fire marshal and under the supervision of the deputy fire marshals, shall:\n\n(1) Investigate fires, structural building collapses, and incidents involving the release of carbon monoxide, other than from a motor vehicle, in accordance with procedures established by the state fire marshal;\n\n(2) Inspect state-owned buildings and other buildings in accordance with procedures established by the state fire marshal;\n\n(3) Assist local fire officials in the promulgation and enforcement of local fire codes;\n\n(4) Review architectural and engineering plans and specifications for compliance with the state fire code; and\n\n(5) Perform such other duties as directed by the state fire marshal or deputy fire marshals.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Saf-C 6000) #13094, eff 8-25-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c6000.html"
